      "evidence": [
        "Behavioral regressions first failed at the unchanged product predecessor: collection blocked foreground access between retirements, all measured recovery callbacks used six actual catalog opens, and bootstrap files were deleted after the actual session stop. Fresh committed tests require foreground completion while parked, exactly two real opens per recovery authorization in the declared protected/synthetic-principal fixture, explicit Native denial before each ID page, and retained key/files when stop intervenes before bootstrap revoke. That fixture count is not a universal production Native open-count claim; the separate full Native journey establishes its actual deadline behavior.",
        "Actual close/reopen denies the old bound cleanup and permits retry only with an observed fresh session; current selected-Incomplete state denies cleanup. Immutable configuration/key/held-file substitutions and bootstrap initialized/empty-subset mode confusion are refused.",
        "Existing real reader-drain, exact historical canonical rekey/sidecar recovery, post-revocation retry, partial-bootstrap process-crash and unknown/hardlink/reparse/mixed-case refusal proofs remain selected. No existing assertion or deadline was weakened."
      ]
    },
